+## 5A. AI-Fit Label and Human-Only Boundary
+
+Every workflow step that uses an AI agent must also carry an AI-fit label, separate from maturity:
+
+~~~text
+AI_GOOD      Agent drafts/extracts/compares; reviewer verifies against evidence.
+AI_LIMITED   Agent assists with a named checkpoint; deterministic service or reviewer owns the result.
+AI_NO_GO     Agent must not produce the governed result.
+~~~
+
+Each step also lists its **human-only decisions** (for example: percent complete, entitlement, award, sequencing logic, measured quantities, acceptance).
+
+Defaults pending per-step review: reading/indexing documents, register population, RFI/report drafting and bid-comparison tables are `AI_GOOD`; programme logic and cost forecasting are `AI_LIMITED`; quantity measurement without calibrated deterministic geometry, entitlement decisions and award decisions are `AI_NO_GO`.
+
+Origin: benchmark comparison in [[08_FEIS_Engineering_Intelligence_Systems/02_Construction_Management/FEIS-CM-RSCH-0002 - ContractorOS Benchmark Extraction and FDG Gap Analysis 2026-11-01|FEIS-CM-RSCH-0002]]. Labels are FDG decisions; they are not copied from the benchmark source.
+
