+## Question Category Taxonomy (Drawing Q&A Benchmarks)
+
+Drawing-question benchmarks should tag each question with one category so weaknesses are visible:
+- sheet reading (title block, notes, legend);
+- tagged-item counting;
+- element detail;
+- schedules;
+- scale and measurement;
+- cross-sheet references;
+- scope (in/out, supply, package);
+- sheet structure (revision, detail counts);
+- **knowing when to stop** (unanswerable from the evidence; correct response is withhold/review-required).
+
+## Rate Reporting Rule
+
+Never report a percentage without its sample size n. Do not rank on categories with very small n. Report counts and measured quantities separately; a total derived from counts must not be presented as measurement accuracy.
+
+State the tolerance convention for measured quantities (for example ±5%) and label it a chosen convention.
+
+## Harness vs Raw Reporting
+
+Report model-only and model-plus-tooling (harness) results separately for the same task, with tool list, version and cost. Harness effect is a measured result, not an assumption.
+
+## Run Variance
+
+Run each evaluated configuration more than once where cost permits and report spread. A single run is directional evidence only.
+
 ## External Benchmark Principle
 
 Open/public benchmarks may be used to compare tooling, but FDG should reproduce scores independently and disclose:
